# Project rules / knowledge

## What this is
- solar-ctl: RPi-based controller for a **Deye inverter** (modbus), publishing to
  Home Assistant energy. Display: 2.79" NV3007 TFT.
- `fw/` — Yocto **kas** firmware build (this is the active part).
- `inv_ctl/` — empty for now; the inverter-controller app. Will be added to the
  image as an `inv-ctl` recipe (placeholder comment in `solar-ctl-image.bb`).
- Target board: **Raspberry Pi Zero W** (`machine: raspberrypi0-wifi`).

## Firmware build (fw/)
- Build with `kas build fw/kas-rpi0.yml` from the repo root (tested with kas 5.5).
- Release: Yocto **wrynose**. No poky: standalone oe-core + our distro conf
  `fw/conf/distro/solar-ctl.conf` (`TCLIBC=musl`, `INIT_MANAGER=systemd`,
  trimmed `DISTRO_FEATURES_DEFAULTS`).
- Layer refs: **branch mode** while pre-production (decided 2026-09): the kas
  file tracks branch tips (`wrynose`; bitbake `"2.18"` — bitbake has no
  wrynose branch and oe-core's sanity checker hard-requires 2.18). Every
  successful build. kas's "branch without commit is unsafe" warnings are
  expected/accepted. To freeze exact refs: `kas lock fw/kas-rpi0.yml` writes
  `fw/kas-rpi0.lock.yml`, which kas auto-applies to every build while it
  exists (update = re-run lock; floating again = delete it) — commit the
  lock file with a release tag. `fw/kas-baseline.yml` is a legacy manual
  reference copy (kas >= 5 has no auto-baseline), superseded by the lock file. **Re-pin `commit:` in
  `fw/kas-rpi0.yml` before tagging the first release.** Last verified good:
  oe-core `883075157987ca300af59185b903d6d1977234c3`,
  meta-raspberrypi `f62c67921474370829d24a4fa01ef88543f3906b`,
  bitbake `f0df79b6b56f6a69067adf974978d9405077f246`,
  meta-oe `14282a02be9c74a1276a7cda7d6c89e054699a11`.
- Use **GitHub mirrors**; `git.yoctoproject.org` is unreachable here (Cloudflare 403):
  use `github.com/openembedded/openembedded-core`, `openembedded/bitbake`,
  `agherzan/meta-raspberrypi`.
- The `solar-ctl` repo entry in the kas file deliberately has **no `url`**: kas
  builds from the working tree, don't "fix" it by adding a url.
- `layers/`, `build/`, `kas-build.log` are generated by kas — gitignored, never edit.
- `SOLAR_WIFI_SSID/PSK/COUNTRY` are set in `fw/kas-rpi0.yml` (`wifi:` section).
  **Never put real WiFi credentials in committed files**; built images bake the
  PSK into a root-only file — never publish built images.

## Yocto/wrynose recipe gotchas (learned the hard way)
- `S = "${WORKDIR}"` is rejected on wrynose — use `S = "${UNPACKDIR}"` and
  `${UNPACKDIR}/<file>` paths for `file://` SRC_URI files.
- A line whose first char is `}` inside a recipe shell/python function breaks
  bitbake's parser (e.g. a `network={...}` heredoc). Use template files + sed.
- `serial-console` is **not** a valid IMAGE_FEATURE on wrynose (it silently
  skips the image recipe). With systemd the serial getty comes automatically
  from `ENABLE_UART=1` + `SERIAL_CONSOLES` (systemd-serialgetty).
- musl + systemd builds fine but bitbake warns it is *experimental* upstream.
- meta-raspberrypi adds `kernel-modules` (= all ~1800 modules) and BT firmware
  to `MACHINE_EXTRA_RRECOMMENDS` on every rpi image; `solar-ctl-image.bb`
  removes them. When a kernel feature is needed, add the specific
  `kernel-module-*` package instead of re-enabling `kernel-modules`.
- `ENABLE_USB_ETH` does not exist; USB gadget mode is `ENABLE_DWC2_PERIPHERAL = "1"`.
- Keep the image minimal: base is `core-image-minimal` + targeted adds only;
  don't pull `packagegroup-core-basic`/`-full-cmdline` style groups.
- WiFi creds: `SOLAR_WIFI_SSID/PSK/COUNTRY` in `fw/kas-rpi0.yml` are baked into
  the image at build time. **Never commit real credentials** to them.
  CI can inject them from Actions secrets (`SOLAR_WIFI_*`) via a generated
  `.kas-wifi-ci.yml` fragment (gitignored). Repo is PUBLIC: only bake a
  lab/guest SSID, never the real home PSK, into CI artifacts/releases.
- **Never use `rm_work_and_downloads`** (use plain `INHERIT += "rm_work"`):
  it puts DL_DIR under `tmp/work/<machine>/<PN>/downloads` and deletes it in
  do_rm_work — breaks recipes built target+native from one tarball (git,
  gettext: `tar: Cannot open` in do_unpack). Its leftover do_fetch sstate
  objects keep stale paths and poison the cache even after reverting; wipe
  `build/tmp` + `build/sstate-cache` if recovering.
- Licenses: `LICENSE_FLAGS_ACCEPTED = "synaptics-killswitch"` is required by
  linux-firmware-rpidistro; keep it set.

## Editor on target
- Use **busybox `vi`** — decided 2026-09 after evaluating classic nvi 1.81.6:
  it fails to build on wrynose's GCC (2003-era code calls `conv_init`/`conv_enc`
  with no prototypes anywhere in the tarball; implicit decls are hard errors
  since GCC 14). Don't retry nvi without backporting the missing prototypes
  (plus stale bundled config.sub — needs gnu-config copy). Also needs db
  compat185 bbappend for `dbopen()`. Not worth it for a Zero W image.

## Device facts
- Zero W WiFi/BT chip: BCM43430 (firmware `linux-firmware-rpidistro-bcm43430`
  comes from the machine conf; driver `brcmfmac` installed in the image).
- Console: UART 115200 8N1; image has dropbear but **root has no password**
  by default (set via serial `passwd`, or lab-only `empty-root-password`).
- Image artifact: `build/tmp/deploy/images/raspberrypi0-wifi/*.wic.bz2`;
  flash with `bmaptool copy` to the raw SD device.
